Procedure
1. Open Remix IDE (https://remix.ethereum.org).
2. Create a new file named Student.sol.
3. Write the Solidity program using struct, dynamic array, and fallback() function.
4. Compile the contract using Solidity compiler version 0.8.20.
5. Open Deploy & Run Transactions.
6. Select Injected Provider – MetaMask and connect to the Sepolia test network.
7. Select StudentData and click Deploy. Confirm the transaction in MetaMask.
8. Under Deployed Contracts, expand StudentData.
9. Use addStudent() to enter student ID, name and age. For example:
   - Student 1: 1, Triveni, 21
   - Student 2: 2, Riya, 20
   - Student 3: 3, Sneha, 21
10. Click Transact and confirm each transaction.
11. Use students(0), students(1) and students(2) to view student details.
12. Click getStudentCount() to display the total number of students.
13. Test the fallback function by sending a transaction with unmatched calldata (0x12345678) and a small Ether value (e.g. 0.001 ETH).
14. Observe and record the gas used and transaction fees for deployment, adding students and fallback execution.
